# The decision log is a pure append-only JSONL file - every write is a new
# line, existing lines are never edited or removed. If two Agent runs ever
# still manage to diverge from the same base despite the sync-to-latest-master
# step in .github/workflows/agent_loop.yml (belt-and-suspenders, since that fix
# should make this rare), git's built-in "union" merge driver is the actually
# correct resolution here: keep every line from both sides rather than asking
# a human (or a CI job with no human present) to pick one over the other.
# Confirmed live Sept 13: a manual reconciliation of exactly this situation
# (two real cycles' worth of decision-log lines, same base) was simply "take
# both, sort by timestamp" - this makes that automatic.
gloaming_agent/decision_log/*.jsonl merge=union

# paper_ledger.json is a full state snapshot (cash/positions/fills), not an
# append-only log - unioning it could produce invalid JSON or a nonsensical
# merged state, so it deliberately keeps git's normal conflict behavior. A
# real conflict there would mean two cycles computed genuinely different
# ledger states from the same starting point, which needs a human to look at,
# not an automatic merge.
